error[NK2605]: This function can fail, because the deadline of `par_iter(within:)` can run out.
  --> tests/par_iter_within_handed_on_unhandled.nika:7:5
   |
 7 |     return ys.iter().zip(xs.par_iter(within: 1.seconds())).count()
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = note: When the deadline runs out, no element starts any more and the step that ends the walk throws `task::TimedOut` (ADR-async-5 D27).
   = help: Add `throws` to `pairs`, or handle it at the call: `… catch { … }`.
1 place that can fail without saying so
